data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":2049,"item_id":"msg_041fda95576ba2f3016b084a10178887d1b214c6903b62038b","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"wren\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Related-capability searches and the complete hand-tie-cord-knot contract establish that its only method is a single-cord overhand knot: it accepts one targetId, not two cord ends. Its non-spilling two-tail trial cannot establish the behavior of a joining bend. hand-twist-fiber-cord makes and tests cords but does not join them. Develop the missing two-cord operation in the current-conversation handoff, reusing existing cord mechanics rather than claiming their reinvention. The supplied records show a second completed cord, but their paged fragments do not establish all current geometry or whether either cord can accommodate a join. Development approval neither performs the join nor grants personal knowledge.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Develop general operation hand-join-fiber-cords, usable by any individually trained actor with applicable owned cords. Parameters: mode attempt/inspect/trial/untie/cancel; two distinct exact cord item IDs for a new attempt; method sheet-bend for the initial version; workId for resumption; target join ID for later operations; trialForce >0 and <=10 N and trialDuration >0 and <=60 s for a trial. One capability covers construction, inspection, testing and reversal. No tools, anchors, extra fiber, second participant or automatic assistance.\\\\nReferences and code reuse: explicitly record reuse of hand-twist-fiber-cord, law fiber-cord@1, for conserved cord geometry, material properties, wear, extension, creep, strand damage and fragment accounting; reuse hand-tie-cord-knot, revision hand-tie-cord-knot@1, handler long.hand-tie-cord-knot, law cord-knot@1, for staged work, reservations, checks and appropriate geometric utilities. Do not reuse its one-cord topology, path formula or non-spilling assertion as a two-cord joining law. Implement a versioned joining-bend law and reusable visual schema as the missing mechanism. Reuse code is not applicant mastery; study this joining method separately. Unsupported material behavior must yield an explicit unsupported-material result, not invented strength.\\\\nPrerequisites: usable bare hands, personally completed study of this operation, two accessible owned unreserved finished cords or physically suitable finished fragments, dry safe footing and clear working space encompassing the manipulated cords. No prerequisite mastery of the two existing abilities is necessary if their mechanics are internal dependencies. Resolve actual condition, centerlines, diameter ranges, existing topology, bend limits, tails and free gripping lengths from the live items at execution, not truncated personal records or nominal length alone. Reject incompatible active knots or reservations without charge; permit separately untying them using applicable learned operations. Disclose costs before confirmation. Study costs 3 worked rounds at 0.2 energy each. Attempt costs at most 4 worked rounds at 0.5 energy each: measure/select bight and crossing, pass second end, wrap and tuck, dress and release-check. Inspection costs 1 round and 0.2 energy; trial 1 round and 0.5 energy; untying at most 2 rounds at 0.5 energy each; cancel is immediate and free. No material is consumed as a fee. Each worked manipulation round applies 0.0005 condition wear to each actually manipulated cord, once; trial additionally applies only the physical damage computed from actual load. Refusals and unworked stages charge nothing.\\\\nThe initial method is a single sheet bend: make a bight in the selected cord, pass the other cord through it, around both bight legs and under its own entering part, dress with the two short ends on the same side. Choose the bight from measured cord suitability, recording the assignment; do not assume equal diameters imply equal suitability. The implementation must resolve finite-width paths and crossings, collision clearance, material bend limits and sequential hand access. A passage needs a 0.02 m clear opening and a retained 0.02 m pinch; dressing must leave each short tail at least 0.02 m plus its local cord width. Final standing parts must independently provide 0.05 m hand grips at least 0.01 m clear of the bend for the requested trial. A tie may be geometrically possible while a two-hand trial is not. Report the specific measured shortfall rather than extending a cord or silently changing method.\\\\nMaintain each cord's own centerline ledger: path inside the join plus free standing part plus free short tail equals that cord's pre-operation centerline, except for separately recorded physically computed stretch, retained creep or breakage. Knot take-up reduces useful joined span, not owned quantity. Preserve both item identities, quantities, origin and processing history; the join is a relation referencing them, not a third stock of cord. Initial tying adds no fiber and removes none. Geometric failure leaves the actually reached physical state, including a loose crossing or released bight; it does not fabricate a completed joint. The joining law must implement finite-width geometry and a material-dependent slip/retention response before execution is enabled. Use existing applicable material properties; if their friction/retention mechanism is missing, implement that minimal mechanism in this handoff, with documented parameters and bounded applicability, rather than rejecting development or inventing a strength result.\\\\nA trial pulls only the two available standing parts in opposition. Achieved force is bounded by the request, 200 N times health/100, each hand's existing grip limit of 10000 N/m times the width it grips, available span and actual failure. Resolve contact sliding, tail movement, tightening, creep, material damage and possible release or rupture for the elapsed loading interval; stop when the grip or joint fails. Reuse the existing material damage routines only within their applicability. Do not copy the overhand strength-reduction formula without establishing applicability to the bend. Record requested and achieved force, actual duration, grip slip, short-tail displacement, before/after geometry and condition, extension, strand damage, and the observed failure location. A holding event means only that this joint held that achieved force for that duration; inspection alone gives no strength, working-load rating or safety guarantee. Rupture produces owned fragments whose lengths, quantity and provenance reconcile exactly with the damaged inputs; no stock disappears or duplicates.\\\\nEach work has an exact workId, actor, input IDs, joining-law version, completed paid stages and persistent physical geometry. Reserve both items atomically before work, and block conflicting use while work or a join binds them. Auto-continuation advances only on actual worked rounds. Interrupted work, unsafe footing, lost reach, insufficient energy or obstructed space pauses before the next charge. Resume requires workId and rechecks actor, ownership, accessibility, material state, hand access and the next stage; paid stages are not repeated. Cancel releases the work reservation exactly once, preserving completed physical changes and actual topology. A complete join remains a linked assembly even after cancellation; an incomplete unretained crossing opens when unsupported, with an observable release event. Death ends active work, releases reservations once and leaves the real cords and any retained join at the death location under existing ownership rules. Neither cancellation, failure nor death refunds paid study, time, energy or wear.\\\\nUntying reverses reachable passes rather than resetting an item. It requires accessible ends, adequate condition and a physically loosenable bend; record jamming or inability to withdraw an end and retain paid progress. No guarantee of restoring original condition or undoing creep. Detached cords preserve their current lengths, damage and histories. No passive loading or strength improvement occurs merely because time passes. Existing material ageing continues while paused or joined; geometry and condition changes invalidate stale measurements. Use existing once-per-round knotted-wear accounting where applicable without double charging the same item. No maintenance materials appear automatically; upkeep is actual inspection, untying or retying with the stated costs. This version excludes unattended loads, attachments to structures and life-safety use. All validated rules execute in code without recurring model approval. Development and review waiting advance neither the world nor work.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":3,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No experience, pleasure, satisfaction or mastery is granted for requesting, registration, development approval, study completion alone, queries or naming. The new operation introduces no direct reward-account writes or automatic mood benefit. Emit evidence of actual completed practice, an observed join, actual untying, or a measured trial, including informative geometric failure. Only personally applicable verified information or legitimate performed practice may be considered by the existing experience evaluator; deduplicate equivalent information and physical practice across this and reused capabilities. Merely inspecting the same unchanged bend does not create new information. Any later pleasure or maintained-satisfaction integration must have explicit event eligibility, modest bounded amounts and shared functional caps, cooldown and decay in code before being enabled; none is granted by this review. Do not change protected accounts, budget, goals, permissions, nutrition or comfort; no physical-comfort benefit is claimed.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Require reusable metadata and observable events for measured geometry, each paid crossing/pass, dressing, release, trial loading, slip, damage, break, pause, cancellation and untying. Include actor/work/join IDs, both referenced item IDs, method and law version, each cord's color and width, centerline paths, over/under crossings, bight radii, free standing spans, short-tail lengths, condition, stage and actual trial force/duration. Render two distinguishable conserved cords, not an unexplained new cord. Events and labels must distinguish incomplete, geometrically infeasible, tied-but-untested, held-at-recorded-load, slipped, jammed and broken states. An attempted crossing or failed trial must never display a success badge, proven strength or successful join. Optional annotations may show measured shortfalls without exposing hidden inventory, resources or unobserved properties. Visual presentation has no independent functional or experience effect.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

